title Update One Session Configuration - Target
actor Caller
participant "Session API" as API
participant "Configuration service" as App
participant "Model service" as Models
database "Session repository" as Repo
Caller -> API : Submit one or more configuration fields
API -> App : Strictly validated request
App -> Repo : Read current configuration
Repo --> App : Session snapshot
opt Model change or thinking enablement requires resolution
  App -> Models : Resolve required model and capabilities
  Models --> App : Validated candidate information
end
App -> App : Normalize submitted values and prepare capabilities
App -> Repo : Lock latest row; merge fields; validate state and capabilities
alt Accepted
  Repo -> Repo : Commit all changes and ordered events, or keep unchanged
  Repo --> App : Authoritative Session snapshot
  App --> API : Response from the same committed snapshot
  API --> Caller : Complete Session
else Rejected
  Repo --> App : No partial changes
  App --> API : Controlled rejection
  API --> Caller : Error
end
note over App,Repo
  Name-only changes may run during execution.
  Execution fields require idle even if unchanged.
  If prepared model differs from the merged target, release
  the lock and prepare again within a bounded retry budget.
  Exhaustion: SESSION_UPDATE_FAILED; no partial write.
  No external I/O under the lock; no inference starts.
end note
@enduml
